  "problem": "$\\int ({cos}^{2}\u2061x-{sin}^{2}\u2061x)\\text{d}x=$",
  "worked_solution": "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta -{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}\u20612\\theta \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({cos}^{2}\u2061x-{sin}^{2}\u2061x)\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}\u20612x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
